  ('Officer', 'GB', "I'd agree. A half plot at Orchard Hill costs sixty-two pounds a year. A full plot is a hundred and ten. There's also a deposit of twenty-five pounds when you start, which you get back when you leave, as long as the plot is left in good condition."),
  ('Caller', 'IE', "That sounds reasonable. What facilities are there on the site?"),
  ('Officer', 'GB', "Orchard Hill has water taps around the site, and every plot has its own water butt for collecting rainwater from the shed roof. There are toilets near the main gate, and a car park. Each plot also comes with a small wooden shed for storing tools. What we don't have yet is a communal building, but the allotment association is raising money for one."),
  ('Caller', 'IE', "Is there anything I'm not allowed to do on the plot?"),
  ('Officer', 'GB', "A few things. You can't keep animals, except for hens, and you need permission for those. Bonfires aren't allowed between April and September, because of complaints from people living nearby. And you must cultivate at least three quarters of your plot. If a plot isn't looked after, we send a warning letter, and if nothing changes after a month, we can give it to someone else on the list."),
  ('Caller', 'IE', "Fair enough. Can I put my name down now?"),
